{"type":"text","timestamp":1788997809660,"sessionID":"ses_f776f37c6ffeLHNTo5P39JtFVe","part":{"id":"prt_088942ce40019I6gmwNLYdXkoO","messageID":"msg_08894292c001FSs9wxZ3mG3q1p","sessionID":"ses_f776f37c6ffeLHNTo5P39JtFVe","type":"text","text":"This is exhaustive over `(bool, bool, bool)`. Let me count:\n- `(true, _, _)`: covers (T,T,T), (T,T,F), (T,F,T), (T,F,F) - 4 cases\n- `(false, true, _)`: covers (F,T,T), (F,T,F) - 2 cases\n- `(false, false, false)`: covers (F,F,F) - 1 case\n- `(false, false, true)`: covers (F,F,T) - 1 case\n\nTotal: 8 cases, which is all of them (2^3). So this should be exhaustive!\n\nThe problem is my `is_tuple_exhaustive` function is too simplistic. Let me fix the logic:","time":{"start":1788997807332,"end":1788997809655}}}
