{"type":"text","timestamp":1788998039944,"sessionID":"ses_f776f37c6ffeLHNTo5P39JtFVe","part":{"id":"prt_08897b0ff0014lDAbyTMz660MJ","messageID":"msg_08897ac40001FW2AKQMU66xrK8","sessionID":"ses_f776f37c6ffeLHNTo5P39JtFVe","type":"text","text":"I see the issue! At line 112, if the line doesn't start with `func_name + '('`, I break. So when parsing Big, after seeing `Big(n) -> n > 100`, the next line is `public atom Tag(atom a)`. This line doesn't start with `Big(`, so I break and return the index.\n\nBut then in the main parse loop, I should continue from that index and parse the next public statement. Let me check the parse method:","time":{"start":1788998037759,"end":1788998039920}}}
