{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1788998069862,"sessionID":"ses_f776f37c6ffeLHNTo5P39JtFVe","part":{"id":"prt_088982e63001DSDrJ7mBjLkO0R","messageID":"msg_088982a29001TVYZdBVPp65OzT","sessionID":"ses_f776f37c6ffeLHNTo5P39JtFVe","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1788998078787,"sessionID":"ses_f776f37c6ffeLHNTo5P39JtFVe","part":{"id":"prt_088982e650010VHExKM6OHI4qc","messageID":"msg_088982a29001TVYZdBVPp65OzT","sessionID":"ses_f776f37c6ffeLHNTo5P39JtFVe","type":"text","text":"I see the issue. My new logic returns idx = the next clause or public statement. But then parse_function's while loop checks `if line.startswith(func_name + '(')`, and since I already returned idx pointing to that next line, the while loop will try to parse it again if it's another clause of the same function, OR break if it's something else.\n\nBut the problem is that when I return from parse_clause_and_switch, parse_function increments idx in the while loop, which skips a line!\n\nActually no, looking at parse_function, it does `idx = self.parse_clause_and_switch(...)`, so it replaces idx with the returned value. Then the while loop condition is checked again.\n\nSo if I return idx pointing to the next clause, the while loop will check if that line starts with `func_name + '('`, and if so, it will parse it again. That's correct.\n\nBut the issue is that for c01, there's only ONE clause for Describe. So after parsing it, what should I return?\n\nLooking at c01:\n```\npublic atom Describe(State s)\nDescribe(s) -> s switch { ... }\n```\n\nLine 0: public statement (parsed by parse_function which adds to functions dict)\nLine 1: Describe(s) -> ... (parsed by parse_clause_and_switch)\n  - This is a switch, so we parse it and return after the closing }\nLine 3+: should be the next line after the switch\n\nAt that point, there's no more code, so I should return a large idx and the parse should finish.\n\nLet me think about what my new parse_clause_and_switch does:\n- It looks at line_idx, which is the clause line\n- It adds the clause to func_def\n- It looks at line_idx + 1 onwards\n- It checks if 'switch' is in the line\n- If yes, it calls parse_switch which handles it and returns\n- If no, it returns when it hits another clause or public statement\n\nSo for c01, the clause line is line 1. Then I look at line 2+. Line 2 has `Describe(s) -> s switch {`, which contains 'switch', so I call parse_switch.\n\nWait, that's wrong! Line 1 IS the clause line with the switch! So when I look at line_idx + 1 = line 2, that's inside the switch body.\n\nThe issue is that the clause and switch are on the same line! Let me look at c01 again:\n\n```\n1: module Verdict\n2: type State = :placed | :shipped | :lost\n3: public atom Describe(State s)\n4: Describe(s) -> s switch {\n5:     :placed  => :new,\n6:     :shipped => :gone,\n7:     :lost    => :unknown\n8: }\n```\n\nSo line 4 is the clause line WITH the switch on the same line. So I need to check if 'switch' is on the clause line itself!\n\nLet me update:","time":{"start":1788998069861,"end":1788998078747}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788998083969,"sessionID":"ses_f776f37c6ffeLHNTo5P39JtFVe","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"toolu_01XnKWKaDAay9ZGUx729GSRY","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck","newString":"    def parse_clause_and_switch(self, func_name: str, line_idx: int, func_def: FunctionDef) -> int:\n        clause_line = self.lines[line_idx].strip()\n        match = re.match(r'(\\w+)\\((.*?)\\)\\s*(?:when\\s+(.+?))?\\s*->', clause_line)\n        if not match:\n            return line_idx + 1\n        \n        pattern = match.group(2)\n        guard = match.group(3).strip() if match.group(3) else None\n        \n        func_def.clauses.append((pattern, guard))\n        \n        # Check if switch is on the same line\n        if 'switch' in clause_line:\n            return self.parse_switch(func_name, line_idx)\n        \n        # Look for a switch in the next few lines\n        idx = line_idx + 1\n        while idx < len(self.lines):\n            line_content = self.lines[idx].strip()\n            \n            # If we hit another clause or public function, stop\n            if line_content.startswith(func_name + '(') or line_content.startswith('public '):\n                return idx\n            \n            # If we find a switch, parse it\n            if 'switch' in line_content:\n                return self.parse_switch(func_name, idx)\n            \n            idx += 1\n        \n        # No switch found, return where we ended\n        return idx","oldString":"    def parse_clause_and_switch(self, func_name: str, line_idx: int, func_def: FunctionDef) -> int:\n        clause_line = self.lines[line_idx].strip()\n        match = re.match(r'(\\w+)\\((.*?)\\)\\s*(?:when\\s+(.+?))?\\s*->', clause_line)\n        if not match:\n            return line_idx + 1\n        \n        pattern = match.group(2)\n        guard = match.group(3).strip() if match.group(3) else None\n        \n        func_def.clauses.append((pattern, guard))\n        \n        # Look for a switch in the next few lines\n        idx = line_idx + 1\n        while idx < len(self.lines):\n            line_content = self.lines[idx].strip()\n            \n            # If we hit another clause or public function, stop\n            if line_content.startswith(func_name + '(') or line_content.startswith('public '):\n                return idx\n            \n            # If we find a switch, parse it\n            if 'switch' in line_content:\n                return self.parse_switch(func_name, idx)\n            \n            idx += 1\n        \n        # No switch found, return where we ended\n        return idx"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n===================================================================\n--- /Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n+++ /Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n@@ -123,8 +123,12 @@\n guard = match.group(3).strip() if match.group(3) else None\n \n func_def.clauses.append((pattern, guard))\n \n+# Check if switch is on the same line\n+if 'switch' in clause_line:\n+    return self.parse_switch(func_name, line_idx)\n+\n # Look for a switch in the next few lines\n idx = line_idx + 1\n while idx < len(self.lines):\n     line_content = self.lines[idx].strip()\n","filediff":{"file":"/Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck","patch":"Index: /Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n===================================================================\n--- /Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-1