{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1788998171085,"sessionID":"ses_f776f37c6ffeLHNTo5P39JtFVe","part":{"id":"prt_08899b9ca001yQ7TtRqblfGnYq","messageID":"msg_08899b526001qB5u182whbQiYt","sessionID":"ses_f776f37c6ffeLHNTo5P39JtFVe","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1788998174260,"sessionID":"ses_f776f37c6ffeLHNTo5P39JtFVe","part":{"id":"prt_08899b9cc001zw2VWGtbjDTrBi","messageID":"msg_08899b526001qB5u182whbQiYt","sessionID":"ses_f776f37c6ffeLHNTo5P39JtFVe","type":"text","text":"So I check unreachable BEFORE unsatisfiable. In c13:\n- First arm: pattern `x`, guard `x > 5 and x < 3`\n- Second arm: pattern `x`\n\nMy `check_unreachable_arms` checks if the first `x` covers the second `x`. It does, so I report unreachable_arm.\n\nBut the spec says: \"An arm every earlier arm already covers is dead. That is `unreachable_arm`, and it is a **warning** rather than an error\".\n\nThe key is \"already covers\". Does the first arm with an unsatisfiable guard actually cover the second arm?\n\nLooking at the spec's semantics, an arm covers another if its pattern matches all values that later arms might match. If the first arm's guard is unsatisfiable, it won't actually match any values, so the second arm is NOT unreachable.\n\nSo I need to account for unsatisfiable guards when checking for unreachable arms. A pattern with an unsatisfiable guard doesn't cover anything.\n\nLet me fix this:","time":{"start":1788998171084,"end":1788998174232}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788998177325,"sessionID":"ses_f776f37c6ffeLHNTo5P39JtFVe","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"toolu_01EYvWpESm1zcAvaQkdW16sy","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck","newString":"    def check_unreachable_arms(self, func_name: str, arms: List[SwitchArm], func_def: FunctionDef):\n        \"\"\"Check for arms covered by earlier arms\"\"\"\n        for i in range(1, len(arms)):\n            current = arms[i]\n            current_pattern = current.pattern.strip()\n            \n            for j in range(i):\n                earlier = arms[j]\n                earlier_pattern = earlier.pattern.strip()\n                \n                # If earlier arm has unsatisfiable guard, it covers nothing\n                if earlier.guard and not self.is_guard_satisfiable(earlier.guard):\n                    continue\n                \n                if self.pattern_covers(earlier_pattern, current_pattern):\n                    self.diagnostics.append('unreachable_arm')\n                    return","oldString":"    def check_unreachable_arms(self, func_name: str, arms: List[SwitchArm], func_def: FunctionDef):\n        \"\"\"Check for arms covered by earlier arms\"\"\"\n        for i in range(1, len(arms)):\n            current = arms[i]\n            current_pattern = current.pattern.strip()\n            \n            for j in range(i):\n                earlier = arms[j]\n                earlier_pattern = earlier.pattern.strip()\n                \n                if self.pattern_covers(earlier_pattern, current_pattern):\n                    self.diagnostics.append('unreachable_arm')\n                    return"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n===================================================================\n--- /Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n+++ /Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n@@ -277,8 +277,12 @@\n for j in range(i):\n     earlier = arms[j]\n     earlier_pattern = earlier.pattern.strip()\n     \n+    # If earlier arm has unsatisfiable guard, it covers nothing\n+    if earlier.guard and not self.is_guard_satisfiable(earlier.guard):\n+        continue\n+    \n     if self.pattern_covers(earlier_pattern, current_pattern):\n         self.diagnostics.append('unreachable_arm')\n         return\n \n","filediff":{"file":"/Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck","patch":"Index: /Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n===================================================================\n--- /Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n+++ /Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n@@ -277,8 +277,12 @@\n for j in range(i):\n     earlier = arms[j]\n     earlier_pattern = earlier.pattern.strip()\n     \n+    # If earlier arm has unsatisfiable guard, it covers nothing\n+    if earlier.guard and not self.is_guard_satisfiable(earlier.guard):\n+        continue\n+    \n     if self.pattern_covers(earlier_pattern, current_pattern):\n         self.diagnostics.append('unreachable_arm')\n         return\n \n","additions":4,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck","time":{"start":1788998177259,"end":1788998177261}},"metadata":{"anthropic":{"caller":{"type":"direct"}}},"id":"prt_08899c62d001BvMpEOQ9VjknRH","sessionID":"ses_f776f37c6ffeLHNTo5P39JtFVe","messageID":"msg_08899b526001qB5u182