{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788998285788,"sessionID":"ses_f7765817fffe5KXGQdzWpZbY01","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"toolu_01MedhjcZT93qEHrjiSbdSsF","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45/PACKET.md","limit":50,"offset":277},"output":"<path>/Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45/PACKET.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n277: ```csharp\n278: public Verdict Describe(Order o)\n279: \n280: Describe(o) -> o.Status switch {\n281:     :placed  => :new,\n282:     :shipped => :gone,\n283:     _        => :unknown\n284: }\n285: ```\n286: \n287: The `_` here is legal because `Status` is an `atom` and the atom universe is open, so the residual\n288: cannot be enumerated — which is the only shape a catch-all is admitted over. Over a *closed*\n289: residual, where the compiler knows the missing case by name, §2 makes `_` an error telling you to\n290: name it — **shipped**, at a switch arm and at a clause head alike.\n291: \n292: For compound conditions, the subject is a **tuple** — which is the clause head's own shape, one\n293: level down:\n294: \n295: <!-- check:\n296: type Disposition = :ack | :dead_letter | :requeue\n297: -->\n298: ```csharp\n299: public Disposition Decide(bool ok, bool permanent, bool redelivered)\n300: \n301: Decide(o, p, r) -> (o, p, r) switch {\n302:     (true,  _,     _)     => :ack,\n303:     (false, true,  _)     => :dead_letter,\n304:     (false, false, false) => :requeue,\n305:     (false, false, true)  => :requeue\n306: }\n307: ```\n308: \n309: Exhaustive with **no catch-all**, and the compiler agrees. An arm takes the clause head's pattern\n310: grammar whole, so it may carry a guard, or be a relational pattern:\n311: \n312: ```csharp\n313: public atom Classify(int n)\n314: \n315: Classify(n) -> n switch {\n316:     m when m < 5 => :retried,\n317:     >= 5         => :exhausted\n318: }\n319: ```\n320: \n321: **The name a guarded arm introduces must be fresh** — `m` above, not `n`. §2's rule reaches here:\n322: a bare name in a pattern *introduces* a name, so an arm written `n when n < 5` where `n` is already\n323: the parameter is `rebinding`, not a match against it. **The guard is not what makes it an error.**\n324: A bare `n` as an arm pattern is rejected with no guard present at all; `m when m < 5` and a plain\n325: `< 5` are both accepted. To match the value `n` already holds, §2's spelling is `== n`.\n326: \n\n(Showing lines 277-326 of 506. Use offset=327 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"```csharp\npublic Verdict Describe(Order o)\n\nDescribe(o) -> o.Status switch {\n    :placed  => :new,\n    :shipped => :gone,\n    _        => :unknown\n}\n```\n\nThe `_` here is legal because `Status` is an `atom` and the atom universe is open, so the residual\ncannot be enumerated — which is the only shape a catch-all is admitted over. Over a *closed*\nresidual, where the compiler knows the missing case by name, §2 makes `_` an error telling you to\nname it — **shipped**, at a switch arm and at a clause head alike.\n\nFor compound conditions, the subject is a **tuple** — which is the clause head's own shape, one\nlevel down:\n\n<!-- check:\ntype Disposition = :ack | :dead_letter | :requeue","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45/PACKET.md","text":"```csharp\npublic Verdict Describe(Order o)\n\nDescribe(o) -> o.Status switch {\n    :placed  => :new,\n    :shipped => :gone,\n    _        => :unknown\n}\n```\n\nThe `_` here is legal because `Status` is an `atom` and the atom universe is open, so the residual\ncannot be enumerated — which is the only shape a catch-all is admitted over. Over a *closed*\nresidual, where the compiler knows the missing case by name, §2 makes `_` an error telling you to\nname it — **shipped**, at a switch arm and at a clause head alike.\n\nFor compound conditions, the subject is a **tuple** — which is the clause head's own shape, one\nlevel down:\n\n<!-- check:\ntype Disposition = :ack | :dead_letter | :requeue\n-->\n```csharp\npublic Disposition Decide(bool ok, bool permanent, bool redelivered)\n\nDecide(o, p, r) -> (o, p, r) switch {\n    (true,  _,     _)     => :ack,\n    (false, true,  _)     => :dead_letter,\n    (false, false, false) => :requeue,\n    (false, false, true)  => :requeue\n}\n```\n\nExhaustive with **no catch-all**, and the compiler agrees. An arm takes the clause head's pattern\ngrammar whole, so it may carry a guard, or be a relational pattern:\n\n```csharp\npublic atom Classify(int n)\n\nClassify(n) -> n switch {\n    m when m < 5 => :retried,\n    >= 5         => :exhausted\n}\n```\n\n**The name a guarded arm introduces must be fresh** — `m` above, not `n`. §2's rule reaches here:\na bare name in a pattern *introduces* a name, so an arm written `n when n < 5` where `n` is already\nthe parameter is `rebinding`, not a match against it. **The guard is not what makes it an error.**\nA bare `n` as an arm pattern is rejected with no guard present at all; `m when m < 5` and a plain\n`< 5` are both accepted. To match the value `n` already holds, §2's spelling is `== n`.\n","lineStart":277,"lineEnd":326,"totalLines":506,"truncated":true}},"title":"Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45/PACKET.md","time":{"start":1788998285750,"end":1788998285771}},"metadata":{"anthropic":{"caller":{"type":"direct"}}},"id":"prt_0889b782e001FLGBEDjdKw51jQ","sessionID":"ses_f7765817fffe5KXGQdzWpZbY01","messageID":"msg_0889b7296001vHGb8GzwERvJWf"}}
