{"type":"text","timestamp":1788998288599,"sessionID":"ses_f7765817fffe5KXGQdzWpZbY01","part":{"id":"prt_0889b7dcb0012V7eT1yWdHXap5","messageID":"msg_0889b79cf0013lbNnIUSZBEALC","sessionID":"ses_f7765817fffe5KXGQdzWpZbY01","type":"text","text":"Aha! This is important: **\"An arm takes the clause head's pattern grammar whole, so it may carry a guard, or be a relational pattern\"**\n\nAnd the example shows:\n```csharp\nClassify(n) -> n switch {\n    m when m < 5 => :retried,\n    >= 5         => :exhausted\n}\n```\n\nSo an arm can be just `>= 5` without a pattern variable. This is a relational pattern! The current parser and checker might not be handling this correctly.\n\nLet me check how I'm parsing the arms:","time":{"start":1788998286795,"end":1788998288585}}}
