{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788998301536,"sessionID":"ses_f7765817fffe5KXGQdzWpZbY01","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"toolu_01DPdZFdE6zNcqAF48Qz1KW5","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45/PACKET.md","limit":20,"offset":419},"output":"<path>/Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45/PACKET.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n419: **A name in an arm pattern is introduced, never matched against.** An arm whose pattern is a bare\n420: name already in scope is `rebinding` — the rule §2 states for clause heads, reaching arms\n421: unchanged, and the paragraph above gives it in full:\n422: \n423: ```csharp\n424: public atom Pick(int n, term e)\n425: \n426: Pick(n, e) -> e switch {\n427:     n => :same,\n428:     _ => :other\n429: }\n430: ```\n431: \n432: — *`Pick` binds `n` twice; a name means one thing in a clause. There is no mutation to assign\n433: with, so rename the second one.* Renaming is one way out; the paragraph above gives the other, for\n434: when you meant to match the value `n` already holds rather than introduce a new name: `== n`.\n435: \n436: **An arm's bindings are its own.** A name bound by one arm's pattern is not in scope in another\n437: arm's body; each arm is a separate branch, and only one of them runs. Reaching for a neighbour's\n438: name is `unbound_variable`:\n\n(Showing lines 419-438 of 506. Use offset=439 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"**A name in an arm pattern is introduced, never matched against.** An arm whose pattern is a bare\nname already in scope is `rebinding` — the rule §2 states for clause heads, reaching arms\nunchanged, and the paragraph above gives it in full:\n\n```csharp\npublic atom Pick(int n, term e)\n\nPick(n, e) -> e switch {\n    n => :same,\n    _ => :other\n}\n```\n\n— *`Pick` binds `n` twice; a name means one thing in a clause. There is no mutation to assign\nwith, so rename the second one.* Renaming is one way out; the paragraph above gives the other, for\nwhen you meant to match the value `n` already holds rather than introduce a new name: `== n`.\n\n**An arm's bindings are its own.** A name bound by one arm's pattern is not in scope in another\narm's body; each arm is a separate branch, and only one of them runs. Reaching for a neighbour's\nname is `unbound_variable`:","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45/PACKET.md","text":"**A name in an arm pattern is introduced, never matched against.** An arm whose pattern is a bare\nname already in scope is `rebinding` — the rule §2 states for clause heads, reaching arms\nunchanged, and the paragraph above gives it in full:\n\n```csharp\npublic atom Pick(int n, term e)\n\nPick(n, e) -> e switch {\n    n => :same,\n    _ => :other\n}\n```\n\n— *`Pick` binds `n` twice; a name means one thing in a clause. There is no mutation to assign\nwith, so rename the second one.* Renaming is one way out; the paragraph above gives the other, for\nwhen you meant to match the value `n` already holds rather than introduce a new name: `== n`.\n\n**An arm's bindings are its own.** A name bound by one arm's pattern is not in scope in another\narm's body; each arm is a separate branch, and only one of them runs. Reaching for a neighbour's\nname is `unbound_variable`:","lineStart":419,"lineEnd":438,"totalLines":506,"truncated":true}},"title":"Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45/PACKET.md","time":{"start":1788998301473,"end":1788998301509}},"metadata":{"anthropic":{"caller":{"type":"direct"}}},"id":"prt_0889bb46b001lVjcObhwNsv5uK","sessionID":"ses_f7765817fffe5KXGQdzWpZbY01","messageID":"msg_0889bb034001357OXFJ33hpw1Y"}}
