{"type":"text","timestamp":1788998447850,"sessionID":"ses_f7765817fffe5KXGQdzWpZbY01","part":{"id":"prt_0889de6ce001l9HzNxYEtpScYV","messageID":"msg_0889de1950013dBczn2T70uuoi","sessionID":"ses_f7765817fffe5KXGQdzWpZbY01","type":"text","text":"Hmm, actually `pattern_covers` is used to check if one arm is unreachable because an earlier arm covers it. In that context, does a bare name count?\n\nLet me think about this carefully:\n- If arm1 has pattern `m` (bare name) and arm2 has pattern `:placed`, is arm2 unreachable?\n- Pattern matching: `m` matches ANY value, including `:placed`. So yes, arm2 is unreachable.\n- But wait, the spec says bare names don't count as coverage...\n\nI think the issue is a confusion between \"coverage\" (for exhaustiveness) and \"matching\" (for unreachability).\n\nFor exhaustiveness: bare names don't count.\nFor unreachability: bare names DO count (they match everything).\n\nSo I need two separate functions:\n1. `pattern_matches` - does pattern p1 match pattern p2 (for unreachability)\n2. `pattern_contributes_to_coverage` - does pattern p1 contribute to coverage (for exhaustiveness)\n\nLet me update this:","time":{"start":1788998444750,"end":1788998447847}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788998451685,"sessionID":"ses_f7765817fffe5KXGQdzWpZbY01","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"toolu_01FWEbL8qCnK8s3jwUPM3qhq","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck","newString":"    \n    def pattern_covers(self, p1: str, p2: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Does pattern p1 cover/match pattern p2? (For unreachability checking)\"\"\"\n        p1 = p1.strip()\n        p2 = p2.strip()\n        \n        # Catch-all covers everything\n        if p1 == '_':\n            return True\n        \n        # Bare names (introducing variables) match anything\n        if self.is_bare_name_pattern(p1):\n            return True\n        \n        # Exact match\n        if p1 == p2:\n            return True\n        \n        return False\n    \n    def is_bare_name_pattern(self, pattern: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Is this a bare name pattern (single lowercase identifier)?\"\"\"\n        pattern = pattern.strip()\n        # A bare name is a single identifier starting with lowercase or _\n        if re.match(r'^[a-z_]\\w*$', pattern):\n            # But NOT if it's an atom or other keyword\n            if pattern.startswith(':') or pattern in ['switch', 'when', 'and', 'or', 'true', 'false', '_']:\n                return False\n            return True\n        return False","oldString":"    \n    def pattern_covers(self, p1: str, p2: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Does pattern p1 cover pattern p2?\"\"\"\n        p1 = p1.strip()\n        p2 = p2.strip()\n        \n        if p1 == '_':\n            return True\n        \n        if p1 == p2:\n            return True\n        \n        return False"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n========================================================