{"type":"text","timestamp":1788998488980,"sessionID":"ses_f7765817fffe5KXGQdzWpZbY01","part":{"id":"prt_0889e88d50015ZJkBTfYoNczDM","messageID":"msg_0889e8454001vXwskM9V57abB7","sessionID":"ses_f7765817fffe5KXGQdzWpZbY01","type":"text","text":"Good! All visible tests pass again. So the current implementation is correct in NOT treating bare names as covering everything for unreachability purposes.\n\nBut then I have a different problem: when is a bare name arm considered to cover another arm?\n\nLooking at the code, I think the answer is: never. Bare name patterns don't result in unreachable_arm because they're not considered to \"cover\" other patterns. But they also don't count towards exhaustiveness.\n\nThis seems to match the spec's intent: bare names match anything at runtime, but for static analysis purposes (covering other arms, contributing to exhaustiveness), they're treated as if they match nothing specific.\n\nOK so the current behavior is correct. Let me now think about other potential issues.\n\nLet me re-examine the visible cases more carefully to see if I'm missing any subtle rules:","time":{"start":1788998486229,"end":1788998488970}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788998491013,"sessionID":"ses_f7765817fffe5KXGQdzWpZbY01","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"toolu_01A1c4MwgpNmMs44zKM5SGEM","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45 && for dir in cases/c*/; do\n  name=$(basename \"$dir\")\n  bs_file=$(find \"$dir\" -name \"in.bs\" -type f)\n  output=$(./switchcheck \"$bs_file\" 2>&1 | sort || true)\n  echo \"$name\"\n  echo \"---\"\n  cat \"$bs_file\"\n  echo \"---\"\n  echo \"Output: $output\"\n  echo \"\"\ndone | head -200"},"output":"c01-exhaustive-closed\n---\nmodule Verdict\ntype State = :placed | :shipped | :lost\npublic atom Describe(State s)\nDescribe(s) -> s switch {\n    :placed  => :new,\n    :shipped => :gone,\n    :lost    => :unknown\n}\n---\nOutput: \n\nc02-catchall-open\n---\nmodule Open\npublic atom Describe(atom s)\nDescribe(s) -> s switch {\n    :placed  => :new,\n    :shipped => :gone,\n    _        => :unknown\n}\n---\nOutput: \n\nc03-inexhaustive\n---\nmodule Missing\ntype State = :placed | :shipped | :lost\npublic atom Describe(State s)\nDescribe(s) -> s switch {\n    :placed  => :new,\n    :shipped => :gone\n}\n---\nOutput: switch_inexhaustive\n\nc04-unreachable\n---\nmodule Shadowed\ntype State = :placed | :shipped\npublic atom Describe(State s)\nDescribe(s) -> s switch {\n    :placed  => :new,\n    :shipped => :gone,\n    :placed  => :again\n}\n---\nOutput: unreachable_arm\n\nc05-tuple-exhaustive\n---\nmodule Decide\npublic atom Route(bool ok, bool permanent, bool redelivered)\nRoute(o, p, r) -> (o, p, r) switch {\n    (true,  _,     _)     => :ack,\n    (false, true,  _)     => :dead_letter,\n    (false, false, false) => :requeue,\n    (false, false, true)  => :requeue\n}\n---\nOutput: \n\nc06-tuple-inexhaustive\n---\nmodule Partial\npublic atom Route(bool ok, bool permanent)\nRoute(o, p) -> (o, p) switch {\n    (true,  _)     => :ack,\n    (false, true)  => :dead_letter\n}\n---\nOutput: switch_inexhaustive\n\nc07-guarded\n---\nmodule Retry\npublic atom Classify(int n)\nClassify(n) -> n switch {\n    n when n < 5 => :retried,\n    >= 5         => :exhausted\n}\n---\nOutput: rebinding\n\nc08-wrong-return\n---\nmodule Wrong\ntype State = :placed | :shipped\npublic int Describe(State s)\nDescribe(s) -> s switch {\n    :placed  => 1,\n    :shipped => :gone\n}\n---\nOutput: return_not_declared\n\nc09-arg-not-accepted\n---\nmodule Calls\npublic bool Big(int n)\nBig(n) -> n > 100\n\npublic atom Tag(atom a)\nTag(a) -> :seen\n\npublic atom Check(int n)\nCheck(n) -> n switch {\n    m when Big(m) => Tag(m),\n    _             => :small\n}\n---\nOutput: arg_not_accepted\n\nc10-switch-in-guard\n---\nmodule Guarded\npublic atom F(atom x)\n\nF(x) when x switch { :a => true, _ => false } -> :yes\nF(x) -> :no\n---\nOutput: switch_in_guard\n\nc11-unbound-variable\n---\nmodule Scopes\npublic term Bad(term e)\n\nBad(e) -> e switch {\n    (:ok, v) => w,\n    (:no, w) => w\n}\n---\nOutput: unbound_variable\n\nc12-vacuous-arm\n---\nmodule Scored\ntype Verdict = :pass | :fail\n\npublic int Score(Verdict v)\n\nScore(v) -> v switch {\n    (:pass, n) => n,\n    :pass      => 1,\n    :fail      => 0\n}\n---\nOutput: vacuous_arm\n\nc13-unsatisfiable-guard\n---\nmodule Graded\npublic int Grade(int n)\n\nGrade(n) -> n switch {\n    x when x > 5 and x < 3 => 0,\n    x                      => 1\n}\n---\nOutput: unsatisfiable_arm_guard\n\n","metadata":{"output":"c01-exhaustive-closed\n---\nmodule Verdict\ntype State = :placed | :shipped | :lost\npublic atom Describe(State s)\nDescribe(s) -> s switch {\n    :placed  => :new,\n    :shipped => :gone,\n    :lost    => :unknown\n}\n---\nOutput: \n\nc02-catchall-open\n---\nmodule Open\npublic atom Describe(atom s)\nDescribe(s) -> s switch {\n    :placed  => :new,\n    :shipped => :gone,\n    _        => :unknown\n}\n---\nOutput: \n\nc03-inexhaustive\n---\nmodule Missing\ntype State = :placed | :shipped | :lost\npu