{"type":"text","timestamp":1788998547899,"sessionID":"ses_f7765817fffe5KXGQdzWpZbY01","part":{"id":"prt_0889f710d001Pbxp2EkDcrTQ77","messageID":"msg_0889f6c90001xwXtMx2svy4vhs","sessionID":"ses_f7765817fffe5KXGQdzWpZbY01","type":"text","text":"OK so the spec is clear: \"Over a *closed* residual, where the compiler knows the missing case by name, §2 makes `_` an error telling you to name it\"\n\nAnd \"the diagnostic names the discarded cases as a head to write instead.\"\n\nSo if the residual is closed (compiler knows the missing cases), using `_` is an error, and the diagnostic should list the missing cases.\n\nBut which diagnostic tag? The message talks about \"the diagnostic names the discarded cases\", which sounds like the message format for `switch_inexhaustive`.\n\nSo I think when there's a `_` on a closed type with missing cases, I should report `switch_inexhaustive`.\n\nLet me update the code:","time":{"start":1788998545677,"end":1788998547887}}}
