{"type":"text","timestamp":1788998631267,"sessionID":"ses_f7765817fffe5KXGQdzWpZbY01","part":{"id":"prt_088a0b5180014T08lRVQ0DjmdE","messageID":"msg_088a0adae001e01AVcQfGSXPK0","sessionID":"ses_f7765817fffe5KXGQdzWpZbY01","type":"text","text":"The regex `[a-z_]\\w*` matches identifiers starting with lowercase or underscore. But wait, this might also match atoms! For example, if the pattern is `:placed`, after removing `==` patterns, `:placed` would still be there, but the regex `[a-z_]\\w*` wouldn't match the `:`, so it would skip the `:` and match `placed`.\n\nIs that a problem? Let me think:\n- Pattern `:placed` - after removing `== patterns`: `:placed`\n- Regex matches: `placed` (the part after `:`)\n- We check `if token and not token.startswith(':')` - but the regex already skips the `:`\n\nSo `placed` would be considered a variable! That's wrong. An atom `:placed` should not introduce a variable.\n\nLet me fix this:","time":{"start":1788998628632,"end":1788998631250}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788998636893,"sessionID":"ses_f7765817fffe5KXGQdzWpZbY01","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"toolu_01GkGtf6R98qC7XtXStigGps","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck","newString":"    def extract_bare_names_from_pattern(self, pattern: str) -> Set[str]:\n        \"\"\"Extract bare identifiers from a pattern (excludes == patterns)\"\"\"\n        # Remove == patterns\n        pattern_no_eq = re.sub(r'==\\s*\\w+', '', pattern)\n        # Remove atoms (anything starting with :)\n        pattern_no_atoms = re.sub(r':\\w+', '', pattern_no_eq)\n        \n        # Extract identifiers\n        names = set()\n        tokens = re.findall(r'\\b[a-z_]\\w*\\b', pattern_no_atoms)\n        \n        for token in tokens:\n            if token and token not in ['_', 'and', 'or', 'when']:\n                names.add(token)\n        \n        return names\n    \n    def extract_bound_vars(self, pattern: str) -> Set[str]:\n        \"\"\"Extract variables bound by this pattern\"\"\"\n        # This includes bare names, not == patterns or atoms\n        bound = set()\n        \n        # Remove == patterns\n        pattern_no_eq = re.sub(r'==\\s*\\w+', '', pattern)\n        # Remove atoms (anything starting with :)\n        pattern_no_atoms = re.sub(r':\\w+', '', pattern_no_eq)\n        \n        tokens = re.findall(r'\\b[a-z_]\\w*\\b', pattern_no_atoms)\n        \n        for token in tokens:\n            if token and token not in ['_', 'and', 'or', 'when']:\n                bound.add(token)\n        \n        return bound","oldString":"    def extract_bare_names_from_pattern(self, pattern: str) -> Set[str]:\n        \"\"\"Extract bare identifiers from a pattern (excludes == patterns)\"\"\"\n        # Remove == patterns\n        pattern_no_eq = re.sub(r'==\\s*\\w+', '', pattern)\n        \n        # Extract identifiers\n        names = s