{"type":"text","timestamp":1788998670609,"sessionID":"ses_f7765817fffe5KXGQdzWpZbY01","part":{"id":"prt_088a151fe0014XtH1PuRDnJFoQ","messageID":"msg_088a14d0a001R8j6L04KLr1ub0","sessionID":"ses_f7765817fffe5KXGQdzWpZbY01","type":"text","text":"Good! So the catch-all handling is working correctly. The switch with catch-all on a closed type is reported as inexhaustive.\n\nNow let me think: is this the correct behavior according to the spec? The spec says catch-all is illegal on closed types. So reporting `switch_inexhaustive` seems like the right diagnostic.\n\nOK so my implementation seems correct.\n\nLet me look for other potential issues. Actually, let me re-check the early return that I fixed. Maybe I didn't fix all of them?","time":{"start":1788998668798,"end":1788998670602}}}
