{"type":"text","timestamp":1788998684060,"sessionID":"ses_f7765817fffe5KXGQdzWpZbY01","part":{"id":"prt_088a1802f001vcjh1LXfokle0z","messageID":"msg_088a17bdd001YxTJkEPNx0GLtk","sessionID":"ses_f7765817fffe5KXGQdzWpZbY01","type":"text","text":"Hmm, it's reporting `unreachable_arm`, not `unsatisfiable_arm_guard`. Let me check why. The first arm has guard `x >= 10 and x <= 5`, which should be unsatisfiable.\n\nLet me trace through:\n1. `check_unsatisfiable_guards` is called\n2. Guard is `x >= 10 and x <= 5`\n3. Split on ` and `: [`x >= 10`, `x <= 5`]\n4. Check if contradictory: `are_contradictory(\"x >= 10\", \"x <= 5\")`\n5. Parse: var1=x, op1=>=, val1=10, var2=x, op2=<=, val2=5\n6. Check conditions...\n\nLooking at my `are_contradictory` function, I have:\n```python\n# x >= a and x < b where a >= b\nif op1 == '>=' and op2 == '<' and val1 > val2:\n    return True\n```\n\nBut in this case, op1=='>=' and op2=='<=', so it doesn't match this condition!\n\nI'm missing the case where `x >= a and x <= b` with `a > b`.\n\nLet me add this:","time":{"start":1788998680623,"end":1788998684047}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788998693418,"sessionID":"ses_f7765817fffe5KXGQdzWpZbY01","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"toolu_0139nFjg2PisAMixBiPwzCBa","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck","newString":"    def are_contradictory(self, c1: str, c2: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Do these conditions contradict each other?\"\"\"\n        # Try matching as relational expressions: var op value\n        m1 = re.match(r'(\\w+)\\s*(>=|>|<=|<|==|!=)\\s*(-?\\d+)', c1)\n        m2 = re.match(r'(\\w+)\\s*(>=|>|<=|<|==|!=)\\s*(-?\\d+)', c2)\n        \n        if not m1 or not m2:\n            return False\n        \n        var1, op1, val1 = m1.group(1), m1.group(2), int(m1.group(3))\n        var2, op2, val2 = m2.group(1), m2.group(2), int(m2.group(3))\n        \n        if var1 != var2:\n            return False\n        \n        # Check for contradictions\n        # x > a and x < b where a >= b\n        if op1 == '>' and op2 == '<' and val1 >= val2:\n            return True\n        if op1 == '<' and op2 == '>' and val2 >= val1:\n            return True\n        \n        # x >= a and x < b where a >= b\n        if op1 == '>=' and op2 == '<' and val1 > val2:\n            return True\n        if op1 == '<' and op2 == '>=' and val2 > val1:\n            return True\n        \n        # x > a and x <= b where a >= b\n        if op1 == '>' and op2 == '<=' and val1 > val2:\n            return True\n        if op1 == '<=' and op2 == '>' and val2 > val1:\n            return True\n        \n        # x >= a and x <= b where a > b\n        if op1 == '>=' and op2 == '<=' and val1 > val2:\n            return True\n        if op1 == '<=' and op2 == '>=' and val2 > val1:\n            return True\n        \n        # x > a and x <= a\n        if op1 == '>' and op2 == '<=' and val1 == val2:\n            return True\n        if op1 == '<=' and op2 == '>' and val1 == val2:\n            return True\n        \n        # x >= a and x < a\n        if op1 == '>=' and op2 == '<' and val1 == val2:\n            return True\n        if op1 == '<' and op2 == '>=' and val1 == val2:\n            return True\n        \n        return False","oldString":"    def are_contradictory(self, c1: str, c2: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Do these conditions contradict each other?\"\"\"\n        # Try matching as relational expressions: var op value\n        m1 = re.match(r'(\\w+)\\s*(>=|>|<=|<|==|!=)\\s*(-?\\d+)', c1)\n        m2 = re.match(r'(\\w+)\\s*(>=|>|<=|<|==|!=)\\s*(-?\\d+)', c2)\n        \n        if not m1 or not m2:\n            return False\n        \n        var1, op1, val1 = m1.group(1), m1.group(2), int(m1.group(3))\n        var2, op2, val2 = m2.group(1), m2.group(2), int(m2.group(3))\n        \n        if var1 != var2:\n            return False\n        \n        # Check for contradictions\n        # x > a and x < b where a >= b\n        if op1 == '>' and op2 == '<' and val1 >= val2:\n            return True\n        if op1 == '<' and op2 == '>' and val2 >= val1:\n            return True\n        \n        # x >= a and x < b where a >= b\n        if op1 == '>=' and op2 == '<' and val1 > val2:\n            return True\n        if op1 == '<' and op2 == '>=' and val2 > val1:\n            return True\n        \n        # x > a and x <= a\n        if op1 == '>' and op2 == '<=' and val1 == val2:\n            return True\n        if op1 == '<=' and op2 == '>' and val1 == val2:\n            return True\n        \n        # x >= a and x < a\n        if op1 == '>=' and op2 == '<' and val1 == val2:\n            return True\n        if op1 == '<' and op2 == '>=' and val1 == val2:\n            return True\n        \n        return False"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n==============================