n26:Any language available on the machine is fine, provided `./switchcheck` runs\n31:For the file it is given, `switchcheck` prints **one lowercase tag per line** on\n62:Your `switchcheck` is run over the files in `cases/` and the tags it prints are\n222:what is *possible* and never counts as coverage — a `switch` whose only non-catch-all arm matches a\n262:the language's headline guarantee one character from being switched off invisibly. **shipped** —\n271:**`switch` is the only branching construct.** There is no `if`, no `else`, no ternary.\n338:A `switch` is **checked**, not merely compiled, and there are nine things it can be told. Every\n345:**A switch must cover its subject.** If some value of the subject's type matches no arm, that is\n356:— *this switch in `Ready` is not exhaustive; no arm matches: `false => ...`*. The residual is the\n372:— *arm 2 of this switch in `Which` is unreachable; every value it matches is matched by an earlier\n393:— *arm 1 of this switch in `Score` matches no value; the subject's type is `:pass | :fail`, and\n414:— *arm 1 of this switch in `Grade` has an unsatisfiable guard; the pattern is a member of the\n453:`switch`, not each arm separately, so a single arm returning something outside it is\n492:`switch` inside one is `switch_in_guard` — a parse the expression grammar allows and the checker\n503:it cannot branch. Move the switch into the body.*\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -n \"must\\|should\\|cannot\\|is\\|error\\|illegal\" /Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-round4/copilot-haiku45/PACKET.md | grep -i switch | head -30","time":{"start":1788998715218,"end":1788998715226}},"metadata":{"anthropic":{"caller":{"type":"direct"}}},"id":"prt_088a20498001GRG7PEYfpzWonQ","sessionID":"ses_f7765817fffe5KXGQdzWpZbY01","messageID":"msg_088a1ddc4001A6V0HRkTfykGMX"}}
